This repository holds the steps that restyle linuxserver.io's OrcaSlicer image for ArtisanHub. It holds no
copy of that image, of its source or of OrcaSlicer. The image it builds contains the works below, each under
its own licence, which this repository and the image keep.

linuxserver.io docker-orcaslicer
  https://github.com/linuxserver/docker-orcaslicer
  Copyright (C) linuxserver.io. GNU General Public License, version 3 (LICENSE).
  The image's base, its start-up scripts, its window manager settings (defaults/labwc.xml) and its web server
  set-up (etc/s6-overlay/s6-rc.d/init-nginx/run) are linuxserver.io's; convert/convert.py changes the last two
  as described in it. This repository's own files are offered under the same licence, GPL-3.0 (LICENSE).

Selkies
  https://github.com/selkies-project/selkies
  The web desktop and its dashboard (usr/share/selkies), Mozilla Public License 2.0 as published with it.
  The ArtisanHub dashboard is a copy of Selkies' own with one stylesheet added; Selkies' files are not changed.

OrcaSlicer
  https://github.com/OrcaSlicer/OrcaSlicer
  Copyright (C) the OrcaSlicer authors. GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 (LICENSES/AGPL-3.0.txt).
  OrcaSlicer is used as linuxserver.io ships it. convert/convert.py changes colour and font values in five of
  its web resource files (resources/web/include/global.css, guide/css/dark.css, guide/css/common.css,
  homepage/css/home.css, dialog/css/common.css); those files, as changed, stay under the AGPL-3.0, and their
  source is the upstream file and the change in convert/convert.py. OrcaSlicer's source is at the address
  above, at the tag of the version named in upstream.env.

Fonts
  Manrope, Sora and JetBrains Mono, SIL Open Font License 1.1: the web fonts from the fontsource packages
  (their licence files are copied beside them in the image), and Manrope and JetBrains Mono for the desktop
  from Debian's fonts-manrope and fonts-jetbrains-mono packages.

GTK and Adwaita
  The ArtisanHub GTK theme imports Adwaita's dark style from the GTK library in the image (LGPL-2.1-or-later)
  and adds its own colours; no Adwaita file is copied.

ArtisanHub design values
  Colours and font choices from artisanhub-ui v0.1.0 (MIT), https://github.com/norjms/artisanhub-ui
